package std.task;

/**
 * An asynchronous computation that may not have finished yet.
 *
 * <p>Calling an {@code async} method returns a {@code Future} of its result
 * without executing any of its body. The body runs as the future is polled,
 * and suspends at each {@code await} whose future is not yet ready:
 *
 * <pre>{@code
 * async int total(&List<String> words) {
 *     int sum = 0;
 *     for (String word : words) {
 *         sum += await lengthOf(word);
 *     }
 *     return sum;
 * }
 * }</pre>
 *
 * <p>The standard library defines what a future is, but not how futures are
 * run. Futures are run by an <em>executor</em>, which is provided by a
 * library: it calls {@link #poll} and, when the result is
 * {@code Poll.Pending}, waits until the task's {@link Waker} is woken before
 * polling the future again.
 *
 * <h2>Borrowing</h2>
 *
 * <p>The future of an {@code async} method holds the method's arguments, so
 * it borrows whatever they borrow for as long as the future exists:
 *
 * <pre>{@code
 * String text = "hello";
 * Future<int> future = lengthOf(&text);
 * text = "bye"; // error: `text` is borrowed by `future`
 * }</pre>
 *
 * <h2>Exceptions</h2>
 *
 * <p>Calling an {@code async} method never throws. Exceptions thrown by its
 * body are thrown by {@code poll}, and therefore by the {@code await}
 * expression that awaits its future.
 *
 * <h2>Cancellation</h2>
 *
 * <p>Dropping a future that has not finished cancels it: it is never polled
 * again, and the values it holds are dropped.
 *
 * <h2>Implementing {@code Future}</h2>
 *
 * <p>{@code poll} makes as much progress as possible without blocking. It
 * returns {@code Poll.Ready} with the result once one is available, and
 * {@code Poll.Pending} otherwise. Before returning {@code Poll.Pending}, it
 * must arrange for {@code cx.waker()} to be woken once polling again can make
 * progress; a future that does not is never polled again.
 *
 * @param <T> the type of the result
 * @see Poll
 * @see Waker
 */
interface Future<T> {
    /**
     * Attempts to make progress without blocking.
     *
     * <p>A future must not be polled again after it has returned
     * {@code Poll.Ready}; the future of an {@code async} method throws an
     * {@link IllegalStateException} if it is.
     *
     * @param cx the context of the task being polled
     * @return {@code Poll.Ready} with the result if the computation has
     *         finished, or {@code Poll.Pending} otherwise
     * @throws Exception any exception thrown by the computation
     */
    mut Poll<T> poll(&mut Context cx) throws Exception;
}
